00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.510 align:start position:0%
arlene foster has been awarded 125 000  pounds in damages after a defamatory  tweet by the tv presenter  dr christian jessen dr jessen tweeted an  unfounded allegation that mrs foster  had been having an extra marital affair  it is a uk record we think in terms of  damages  awarded for defamation by social media  it was december 2019 when these  entirely false allegations began  circulating that arlene foster  was engaged in an extra martial affair  with one of her security detail  and that allegation was tweeted by dr  jessen  despite mrs foster's lawyers advising  him to take it down he didn't do so  for two weeks during which time she  commenced these legal proceedings  she herself told the court that it was  humiliating to have what she described  as the  most important relationship in the world  to her trashed in this way  the dup leader and first minister who's  been married to her husband brian  for 26 years explained how she had to  explain to her two eldest children and  to her 85 year old mother  about these matters just two days before  christmas and she said she didn't think  it was a coincidence that this  tweet had and that allegation had  circulated at a time when she was  involved in efforts to restore  devolved government indeed her lawyer  paul tweed has described this as a very  significant moment indeed  for women in public life  dr jessen has been offered every  opportunity  to do the right thing in this regard  from the outset  but he has pointedly failed to do so  my client is grateful to the court  for this total vindication  which hopefully will also act  as an encouragement and a watershed  for all women in public life who have  been subjected  to similar attacks on social media  in launching his own defense at a very  late stage  dr jessen said he was surprised to learn  that the legal action  had reached an advanced stage he said he  had withdrawn from public life gone to  live with his parents  because he was suffering from mental  illness but the judge said there was no  medical evidence of any nature to  substantiate that claim  and he described dr jessen's claims of  living with his parents and therefore  not receiving the necessary legal  documents  as unsatisfactory and unconvincing the  judge described this  as a highly libelous and grossly  defamatory  tweet before proceeding uh to award the  damages he has 125 thousand pounds  some consolation and vindication perhaps  for mrs foster  on the very day she formally steps down  as the leader of the democratic unionist  party
 

